<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Supervise Hammerspoon: launchd restarts it the moment it dies, and it is the ONLY launcher.

  Why (docs/research/screenshot-pipeline-2026-09-10.md §F1, §F1b, §F6, §F9 K3):
  - 2026-09-09 18:55 a fleet census SIGTERMed Hammerspoon; as a plain Login Item nothing restarted
    it, and the ⌘⇧4 → clipboard pipeline was dead for 5.4 h.
  - KeepAlive re-forks a MATURE job in ~1 ms at the DEFAULT ThrottleInterval (K3 refuters, n=15).
    ThrottleInterval is deliberately absent: =1 would only turn a start-up crash into a 1 Hz loop.
  - ProgramArguments is the binary itself, never a wrapper: TCC grants (Accessibility, Screen
    Recording) are keyed to the signed bundle, and `supervise.sh install` asserts both on this exact
    launch provenance before it removes the Login Item.
  - A Program-launched agent bypasses LaunchServices' single-instance check, so the Login Item must
    go (supervise.sh does it) or login would start a second instance (§F8 item 3).

  Install / remove ONLY through scripts/supervise.sh (bootstrap/bootout, never load/unload).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>org.hammerspoon.Hammerspoon.keepalive</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Applications/Hammerspoon.app/Contents/MacOS/Hammerspoon</string>
  </array>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Interactive</string>
  <key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key>
  <string>Aqua</string>
  <key>AssociatedBundleIdentifiers</key>
  <array>
    <string>org.hammerspoon.Hammerspoon</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
